# Derived intermediates. Large, rebuildable from data/ + the SatGen trees via
# a driver in scripts/. Kept locally so the repo is self-contained on this
# machine; GitHub carries the recipe, not the bytes.
results/

# Large binary data anywhere in the tree. Small text inputs under data/
# (catalogs, kinematics, published limit curves) are committed and are the
# provenance-critical layer; force-add one of these only if it is genuinely
# small and genuinely an input:  git add -f data/<source>/<file>
*.npz
# Exception: the Symphony / Milky-Way-est per-host reductions (1.2 MB total).
# They are the *input* to `make_h5.py sims`, not a derived product, and without
# them a fresh clone cannot rebuild those two catalogs at all.
!data/symphony/**/*.npz
*.npy
# PPPC4DM annihilation tables: 40 MB of a public literature release, pinned by
# sha256 in data/fermi_legacy/PPPC4DM/VERSION and checked by
# tests/test_pppc4dm_pin.py rather than committed. Scoped to that tree so a
# small .dat input elsewhere under data/ is still committable by default.
data/fermi_legacy/PPPC4DM/**/*.dat
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.fits
*.pkl

# Job logs. scripts/<name>.sh writes stdout to scripts/<name>_out/.
# The directories themselves must survive a fresh clone: SLURM resolves
# #SBATCH --output= against the submission directory at dispatch time, before
# the script body's mkdir ever runs, so a missing log directory silently drops
# every array task. Ignore the contents, keep the .gitkeep. (Ignoring the
# directory itself would not work -- git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation for a file inside it never matches.)
scripts/*_out/*
!scripts/*_out/.gitkeep
slurm-*.out
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*~

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
